; stashload.eval - unsaved editor work survives a save LOADED on another level
; (code-review C298). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 31, on a scratch copy
; of dungeon-demo; `stashtest` is renamed to this worktree's save.
;
; A save made on eval_arena; then crypt1, where a wall is painted at 9,1 and
; not saved. Loading the save lands on eval_arena, which leaves crypt1 by the
; "throwaway baseline" door: its DYNAMIC state is rightly dropped, but its map
; used to go with it - the paint gone, with no prompt and no log line. Now the
; map is stashed whoever is leaving, when it differs from its file: savemap
; writes crypt1 from that stash, and going back to crypt1 finds the wall.
;
; THE CONTROL on the measure itself: the active map reads `edited` after the
; paint, `clean` after an undo puts the file's square back (a comparison, not a
; latch an edit sets), and `edited` again after the paint is redone.

logecho on
reset
save stashtest
goto crypt1
echo --- before ---
mapinfo
stashes
editor drag walls wall_marble 9 1
echo --- painted ---
mapinfo
stashes
undo
echo --- undone ---
stashes
editor drag walls wall_marble 9 1
echo --- repainted ---
stashes
mappage close
load stashtest
echo --- loaded ---
stashes
savemap
goto crypt1
echo --- returned ---
mapinfo
stashes
echo --- end ---
